# Submit or stop a 1-D kinematic drawer playback (2026-09-06 visual backend).
#
# Only the electrical-mezzanine db1 drawer (kind=drawer) accepts playback today.
# While a START playback is active the cabinet plugin bypasses that drawer's
# latch/spring/coupling physics and drives its prismatic rail joint along a
# piecewise-linear position schedule (trajectory) so an external visual
# executor can open/close the drawer kinematically without a force seal.
#
# Ownership contract (mirrors the other cabinet services):
#   * control_id + operation_lease_id must be valid; a playback already owned by
#     a DIFFERENT lease is refused (stale tasks cannot hijack the rail).
#   * START  arms the schedule and begins playing; accepted does not mean the
#     motion finished -- completion is verified by the drawer's live state.
#   * HOLD   freezes the drawer at the current playback position.
#   * RELEASE ends playback ownership; the drawer returns to plugin default
#     control parked at its current position.
# Trajectory rules (rejected otherwise):
#   * single joint, positions in metres along the rail axis 0;
#   * header.stamp is the (sim) time the schedule starts from, time_from_start
#     must be finite and strictly increasing, first point >= 0;
#   * no NaN/Inf; every position inside the drawer joint limits;
#   * the drawer is driven kinematically -- never jump from an arbitrary start:
#     the first sample must be within a small window of the current position.
uint8 COMMAND_START = 0
uint8 COMMAND_HOLD  = 1
uint8 COMMAND_RELEASE = 2

uint8 command
string control_id
string operation_lease_id
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory trajectory
---
bool success
string message
# Measured drawer rail position when the request was applied (metres).
float64 position
# START: true once the whole schedule has already finished at apply time.
# HOLD/RELEASE: whether playback had completed before ownership ended.
bool finished
